A||||5||mbramble||Other Donor Cars for Fiero Parts||||1||
Z||000000||mbramble||08-16-2001||08:46 PM||||I think it would be good to come up with a list of other cars that have parts that fit our Fieros.  Maybe if we come up with a good list, Ogre can post it in his Cave.  There are very few Fieros in the two u-pull-it yards around here and they have been just about stripped to nothing.  On a recent trip I just started looking around at other cars in the GM section.  I was able to get a headlight module and headlight motor from an 88 Firebird.  Just a couple of days ago I got a power mirror from an 85 Camaro.  I also noticed that it had the identical window and lock motors used in our cars.  I am going back in the morning with my drill and drill out the rivets and bring them home for spares.  Anyway, here's a start:<P>Power window motors (don't know about the regulator part) -- 85 Camaro<BR>Power door lock 'motors' -- 85 Camaro<BR>Mirrors -- 85 Camaro (though if you are matching it to a Fiero mirror, you need the 'spacer' that mounts between the mirror and door. If replacing both mirrors you may be able to use the Camaro spacers)<BR>Power mirror switch -- 85 Camaro<BR>Power door lock switches -- 85 Camaro<BR>Headlight motors (87+) -- 88 Firebird<BR>Headlight module (87+) -- 88 Firebird<P>I'm sure ranges of years of Camaros and Firebirds will have useable parts but I don't know enough about them to know what those ranges would be.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Philphine||08-16-2001||09:09 PM||||i get a lot of that info from my local library. they have interchange manuals up to '86. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||08-16-2001||09:10 PM||||Auto Tranny Mounts are pretty much the same in all midsized family cars that have the 3 speed... Ponitac 6000, Buick Centry...||||reg||1
Z||000003||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-16-2001||09:14 PM||||Axles - mid 80's FWD  (skylark,6000,etc)<BR>lower Balljoints - mid 80's FWD  (skylark,6000,etc)<BR>Upper balljoints (front) chevette<BR>Struts - mid 80's FWD  (skylark,6000,etc)<BR>(may need to change the top)<P>PS great idea for a thread  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||08-16-2001||10:33 PM||||Don't forget people, 88's are unique on some parts, so if you know they're only good for certain years (suspension, brakes, etc) then how about making note of it.  Window motors etc. are pretty self explanatory.||||reg||1
